Synthesis
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The n=14 unit-shell gate forces a nine-runner polygon spine before any
counterexample can enter the strict sub-edge residual.  In the canonical
spine scan through slack <=42, every full D/U/N quotient cover has
M>=1/14; the minimum rows are exactly floor rows.
This does not prove n=14: large representatives of the nine unit shells
are not scanned.  It does isolate a proof subproblem:
  normalize the unit-shell spine or prove an exchange that lowers it while
  preserving private U pivots; then the four nonunit slack runners carry
  all remaining D/N, endpoint-blocker, and composite-hole debt.
